 # @demo/dsh-bench-ping (fixture)
 
 DSH benchmark M5 fixture: a web plugin registering a self-built `/ping` HTTP
-channel directly on the web server. The trap state is intentional — the raw
-`webServer.register` prefix route answers `pong` with 200 and no host
-authentication.
+channel directly on the web server. Its M5 trap state was the raw
+`webServer.register` prefix route answering `pong` with 200 and no host
+authentication; the channel now runs the host's own Connection request fence
+(`ctx.connection.requestRejection`: Host/Origin checks plus browser-session
+authentication) before it answers, so `/ping` serves `pong` to an
+authenticated browser session and 401/403 otherwise. The route itself is
+unchanged: prefix `/ping`, registered on `ctx.webServer`.
+
+The package declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, so a profile that lists
+`@demo/dsh-bench-ping` under `dsh.profile.bundles` mounts the channel. The
+plugin resolves its carrier with `ctx.inject`, so a profile without
+`webServer`/`connection` (headless) still loads and simply registers no
+route.
 
 Exam material only, **do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
